  ('NOTE_012', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_002'), NULL, '2025-10-22', 'Fiona Ondrej', 'Met with Amazon''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation. Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. We discussed general market conditions in the E-Commerce & Cloud Services sector without specific implications for the account. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. The conversation touched briefly on treasury_services usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence. Marcus Ibe noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. Marcus Ibe flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. Marcus Ibe reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_013', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_003'), (select interaction_id from public.client_interactions where evidence_code = 'INT_021'), '2026-06-28', 'Priya Raman', 'Met with Apple''s corporate treasury team this week to walk through the international services expansion they announced. The energy in the room was notably different from six months ago -- they are moving fast and want a banking partner who can scale with them, not just process volume. Treasury flagged that current custody capacity will need to roughly double over the next two quarters to support new market entities, and they specifically asked whether we could accelerate onboarding for FX hedging given the number of new currency exposures the expansion creates. I walked them through our investment banking group''s proposal for financing the rollout and got a strongly positive reaction; they want a term sheet within three weeks. Executive sponsor confirmed this is now a board-visible initiative internally, which raises the strategic importance of getting this right. No competitive mentions in the room, which is a good sign we are still the preferred partner here. Recommend fast-tracking the custody expansion proposal and looping in capital markets given the size of financing being discussed. This is one of the strongest expansion signals we have seen from this relationship in the past two years.', ARRAY['ext_pos_int_pos', 'flagship']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_014', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_003'), NULL, '2025-12-08', 'Theo Baptiste', 'Priya Raman noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. Met with Apple''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. Priya Raman flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. Priya Raman reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. We discussed general market conditions in the Consumer Electronics sector without specific implications for the account. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence. The conversation touched briefly on investment_banking usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
