  ('NOTE_019', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_004'), (select interaction_id from public.client_interactions where evidence_code = 'INT_031'), '2026-06-22', 'Colin Ashford', 'Notable inbound outreach from UnitedHealth''s CFO office this week, prompted by the regulatory scrutiny and cost-reduction program they announced publicly. Rather than a defensive posture, the tone was opportunistic -- they are looking for a banking partner to help structure financing and provide transformation advisory as they reorganize segments of the business in response to the regulatory environment. This is a meaningful shift from prior conversations, which had been largely transactional around treasury services. Core relationship revenue has been essentially flat for the past six quarters, so this proposal represents genuine incremental opportunity rather than defense of an existing book. There is moderate competitive pressure -- they mentioned at least one other bank is also being asked to scope a similar proposal -- so responsiveness matters here. Recommend assembling a joint treasury and investment banking team to move quickly; the executive sponsor relationship is strong and this could meaningfully deepen the relationship tier if we win the mandate.', ARRAY['ext_neg_int_opp', 'flagship']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_020', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_004'), NULL, '2025-04-22', 'Colin Ashford', 'Met with UnitedHealth Group''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. We discussed general market conditions in the Managed Health Care sector without specific implications for the account. The conversation touched briefly on treasury_services usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. Colin Ashford noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. Colin Ashford flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation. Colin Ashford reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
