  ('NOTE_028', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_005'), NULL, '2025-04-12', 'Naomi Kessler', 'We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. The conversation touched briefly on lending usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. Renata Souza noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. Met with CVS Health''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. Renata Souza reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation. Renata Souza flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. We discussed general market conditions in the Health Care & Pharmacy sector without specific implications for the account.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_029', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_006'), (select interaction_id from public.client_interactions where evidence_code = 'INT_048'), '2026-06-26', 'Theo Baptiste', 'Sobering conversation with Exxon Mobil''s corporate finance team following confirmation that we lost the bond issuance mandate to Harrow & Vance Capital. This is despite the strong earnings and expansion news the company announced publicly this quarter -- if anything, that public strength appears to be benefiting our competitor rather than us. The client was direct that Harrow & Vance has been more aggressive on both pricing and coverage intensity, and is now also leading two other financing conversations that used to be ours to lose. Relationship revenue has been declining for three consecutive quarters and the trade finance renewal is now stalled pending a competing term sheet. Risk scores have moved up meaningfully as our share of wallet concentrates into fewer, smaller products. This is a clear case where the company''s public good news is not translating into a stronger relationship for us -- quite the opposite. Recommend an urgent relationship-risk review and a senior banker introduction before we lose further ground.', ARRAY['ext_pos_int_neg', 'flagship']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_030', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_006'), NULL, '2025-03-02', 'Grant Elias', 'Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. Theo Baptiste reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. Theo Baptiste flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. The conversation touched briefly on fx usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. Met with Exxon Mobil''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. Theo Baptiste noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. We discussed general market conditions in the Oil & Gas sector without specific implications for the account. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
