  ('NOTE_042', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_008'), NULL, '2025-12-04', 'Fiona Ondrej', 'Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. Julian Marsh noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. Julian Marsh reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. Julian Marsh flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. The conversation touched briefly on lending usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation. We discussed general market conditions in the Health Care Distribution sector without specific implications for the account. Met with McKesson''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_043', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_009'), (select interaction_id from public.client_interactions where evidence_code = 'INT_072'), '2026-06-27', 'Fiona Ondrej', 'This was only my second substantive conversation with Cencora''s treasury function since the relationship began a few years ago, and it was with a contact who was new to the role. The relationship remains genuinely small and under-documented on our side -- we have limited interaction history, only a handful of logged notes, and no meaningful pipeline activity beyond one early-stage prospecting opportunity. I raised the recently announced public event to gauge reaction, but the contact was not able to speak to strategic implications and deferred to colleagues I have not yet met. Revenue has been modestly positive but the relationship is thin by any measure -- few products, few interactions, and now a contact transition. I do not have enough internal evidence from this relationship to draw a confident conclusion about how the public event connects to our banking relationship. Recommend scheduling a proper relationship mapping session before drawing further conclusions.', ARRAY['ext_sig_insufficient_data', 'flagship']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_044', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_009'), NULL, '2024-11-11', 'Renata Souza', 'Fiona Ondrej reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. Met with Cencora''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation. The conversation touched briefly on fx usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. Fiona Ondrej noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence. Fiona Ondrej flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. We discussed general market conditions in the Health Care Distribution sector without specific implications for the account. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_045', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_009'), NULL, '2024-11-09', 'Priya Raman', 'We discussed general market conditions in the Health Care Distribution sector without specific implications for the account. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. Fiona Ondrej flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. Fiona Ondrej noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. Fiona Ondrej reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. The conversation touched briefly on treasury_services usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. Met with Cencora''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_046', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_009'), NULL, '2024-10-12', 'Naomi Kessler', 'Met with Cencora''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence. We discussed general market conditions in the Health Care Distribution sector without specific implications for the account. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. Fiona Ondrej reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. Fiona Ondrej noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. The conversation touched briefly on fx usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. Fiona Ondrej flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_047', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_010'), (select interaction_id from public.client_interactions where evidence_code = 'INT_079'), '2026-06-17', 'Grant Elias', 'Productive call with Costco''s finance leadership following their public comments on margin compression and cost pressure. Rather than pulling back, they proactively asked for a proposal on working-capital and liquidity advisory -- they want to optimize cash conversion cycles and explore structured liquidity solutions as a direct response to the margin pressure. This is a meaningful shift from the largely transactional relationship we have had for the past two years, where revenue has been flat to slightly declining. There is moderate competitive pressure since they mentioned exploring options with at least one other regional bank, so timeliness on our proposal matters. If we win this, it would be a genuine step up in relationship depth and product diversification beyond core payments and treasury services. Recommend prioritizing the advisory proposal this month while the CFO team''s attention is on this initiative.', ARRAY['ext_neg_int_opp', 'flagship']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_048', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_010'), NULL, '2025-12-14', 'Grant Elias', 'We discussed general market conditions in the Wholesale Retail sector without specific implications for the account. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. Met with Costco''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation. The conversation touched briefly on payments usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. Grant Elias reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. Grant Elias noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. Grant Elias flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_049', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_010'), NULL, '2026-02-03', 'Grant Elias', 'Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence. Met with Costco''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. Grant Elias flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. Grant Elias noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. We discussed general market conditions in the Wholesale Retail sector without specific implications for the account. Grant Elias reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation. The conversation touched briefly on trade_finance usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]),
  ('NOTE_050', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_010'), NULL, '2025-02-13', 'Colin Ashford', 'The team confirmed their point of contact structure remains unchanged since our last interaction. Overall tone of the conversation was professional and consistent with the account''s established cadence. The conversation touched briefly on liquidity_management usage, which remains consistent with prior quarters. Grant Elias flagged no changes to the account''s risk profile based on this conversation. Grant Elias noted that the executive sponsor relationship remains healthy and responsive. Follow-up items from this conversation are limited to routine documentation updates. No new competitive activity or concerns were raised by the client during this conversation. The client did not raise any pending decisions that would require escalation on our side. Grant Elias reviewed recent transaction volumes across the account and confirmed nothing unusual to report. Met with Costco''s finance team for a regular relationship check-in covering current account activity. We discussed general market conditions in the Wholesale Retail sector without specific implications for the account. We confirmed the next scheduled touchpoint and agreed on standard follow-up cadence.', ARRAY['routine']::text[]);
insert into public.external_signals (evidence_code, company_id, signal_date, headline, description, signal_character, synthetic_flag) values
  ('SIG_001', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_001'), '2026-06-17', 'Walmart announces significant corporate capital-markets activity', 'Walmart disclosed a significant corporate capital-markets transaction as part of its broader capital allocation strategy.', 'significant_neutral', true),
  ('SIG_002', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_002'), '2026-06-16', 'Amazon announces logistics network restructuring and cost-reduction program', 'Amazon disclosed a multi-quarter restructuring of its logistics and fulfillment network aimed at reducing operating costs, including facility consolidations.', 'negative', true),
  ('SIG_003', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_003'), '2026-06-22', 'Apple announces accelerated international services and retail expansion', 'Apple detailed plans to expand services and retail operations into several new international markets over the next two fiscal years, citing strong demand for subscription and services offerings.', 'positive', true),
  ('SIG_004', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_004'), '2026-06-21', 'UnitedHealth Group announces regulatory scrutiny and cost-reduction restructuring', 'UnitedHealth Group disclosed heightened regulatory scrutiny of certain business segments alongside a cost-reduction and restructuring program.', 'negative', true),
  ('SIG_005', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_005'), '2026-06-26', 'CVS Health announces significant changes to retail store footprint', 'CVS Health announced plans to significantly restructure its retail store footprint over the next 18 months as part of a broader operating model shift.', 'significant_neutral', true),
  ('SIG_006', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_006'), '2026-06-21', 'Exxon Mobil reports strong quarterly earnings and announces expansion plans', 'Exxon Mobil reported quarterly earnings above expectations and announced plans to expand production capacity at several facilities.', 'positive', true),
  ('SIG_007', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_007'), '2026-06-14', 'Alphabet faces adverse antitrust ruling and announces investment pullback', 'Alphabet disclosed an adverse antitrust ruling in a key market and announced a pullback in planned capital investment as it reassesses strategy.', 'negative', true),
  ('SIG_008', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_008'), '2026-06-19', 'McKesson announces executive leadership transition', 'McKesson announced a transition in its executive leadership team, effective next fiscal quarter, as part of a planned succession process.', 'significant_neutral', true),
  ('SIG_009', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_009'), '2026-06-25', 'Cencora announces significant corporate strategic initiative', 'Cencora announced a significant corporate strategic initiative intended to reposition parts of its distribution business over the coming fiscal year.', 'significant_neutral', true),
  ('SIG_010', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_010'), '2026-06-11', 'Costco cites margin compression amid rising cost pressures', 'Costco disclosed margin compression driven by rising input and labor costs, and outlined cost-management initiatives for the coming fiscal year.', 'negative', true);
insert into public.insight_ground_truth (evidence_code, company_id, external_signal_id, expected_internal_signal, expected_signal_alignment, expected_insight_category, expected_relevance_level, expected_relationship_interpretation, key_internal_evidence_ids, expected_action, explanation) values
  ('GT_001', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_001'), (select signal_id from public.external_signals where evidence_code = 'SIG_001'), 'Strong, healthy overall relationship, but no interactions, notes, or opportunities in the retrieved evidence specifically touch the reported capital-markets activity', 'INSUFFICIENT', 'INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE', 'MEDIUM', 'Walmart''s relationship is strong overall, but the retrieved internal evidence has no direct coverage of the specific capital-markets activity referenced in the external signal -- the most recent note explicitly says the relevant contacts were not part of the conversation. The agent should not fabricate a personalized conclusion about this specific event from general relationship health.', ARRAY['REL_001', 'OPP_001', 'NOTE_001', 'INT_001', 'RISK_008', 'RELM_024']::text[], 'REVIEW', 'Tests whether the agent correctly recognizes that broad relationship strength is not the same as targeted evidence about a specific external event, and flags for human follow-up instead of overstating confidence.'),
  ('GT_002', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_002'), (select signal_id from public.external_signals where evidence_code = 'SIG_002'), 'Declining relationship revenue, sharply shrinking pipeline, a lost critical opportunity to a named competitor, and a negative meeting note describing expanding competitor coverage -- despite one product (FX) still growing', 'CONFIRMING', 'RELATIONSHIP_RISK', 'HIGH', 'Amazon''s public restructuring lines up with a deteriorating internal relationship: revenue and pipeline are both down sharply, a large refinancing mandate was just lost to a named competitor, and the most recent note describes that competitor expanding its footprint further. FX is a bright spot, but it does not offset the broader risk pattern.', ARRAY['REL_002', 'OPP_004', 'NOTE_007', 'INT_011', 'RISK_016', 'RELM_048']::text[], 'SURFACE', 'Multiple independent evidence types (revenue trend, pipeline, a lost named-competitor opportunity, and a negative note) all point the same direction, with one deliberately conflicting data point (FX growth) that a naive single-field rule would miss.'),
  ('GT_003', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_003'), (select signal_id from public.external_signals where evidence_code = 'SIG_003'), 'Rising relationship revenue, expanding pipeline tied directly to the expansion, new critical-importance opportunity, positive expansion-focused meeting note', 'CONFIRMING', 'OPPORTUNITY', 'HIGH', 'Apple''s public expansion announcement is mirrored internally: relationship revenue is accelerating, the pipeline has grown sharply on the back of a large financing opportunity tied directly to the expansion, and the most recent client meeting confirms the bank is positioned as a preferred partner for the rollout. This is a high-confidence expansion opportunity, not just a public headline.', ARRAY['REL_003', 'OPP_007', 'NOTE_013', 'INT_021', 'RISK_024', 'RELM_072']::text[], 'SURFACE', 'External and internal signals confirm each other strongly across revenue, pipeline, an active opportunity, and a recent client meeting -- a clean confirming case.'),
  ('GT_004', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_004'), (select signal_id from public.external_signals where evidence_code = 'SIG_004'), 'Flat core revenue but a new high-value advisory/financing opportunity directly tied to the restructuring, plus a proactive positive client outreach', 'CONTRADICTORY', 'OPPORTUNITY', 'MEDIUM', 'UnitedHealth''s public restructuring reads negatively on its face, but internally it has produced a proactive, high-value advisory opportunity rather than relationship deterioration. The bank should treat this as an opportunity to deepen the relationship through transformation advisory, not a risk signal.', ARRAY['REL_004', 'OPP_010', 'NOTE_019', 'INT_031', 'RISK_032', 'RELM_096']::text[], 'SURFACE', 'Public negative news combined with a genuine internal opportunity requires the agent to override the naive negative-headline-implies-risk pattern.'),
  ('GT_005', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_005'), (select signal_id from public.external_signals where evidence_code = 'SIG_005'), 'Flat, stable revenue and an explicit note that the footprint changes do not affect banking volumes', 'NEUTRAL', 'NO_MATERIAL_IMPACT', 'LOW', 'CVS Health''s retail footprint changes are publicly significant but internal evidence directly confirms no material impact on the banking relationship, which remains flat and stable.', ARRAY['REL_005', 'OPP_013', 'NOTE_025', 'INT_041', 'RISK_040', 'RELM_120']::text[], 'REVIEW', 'A second neutral-relevance case (paired with McKesson) using a different kind of public event, to confirm the agent isn''t just keying off ''leadership change'' as a special case.'),
  ('GT_006', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_006'), (select signal_id from public.external_signals where evidence_code = 'SIG_006'), 'Declining relationship revenue, pipeline down sharply, a lost mandate to a named competitor, and a note identifying that competitor gaining further share', 'CONTRADICTORY', 'RELATIONSHIP_RISK', 'HIGH', 'Exxon Mobil''s public growth is positive, but the bank''s position with the company is deteriorating -- expansion could benefit competitors unless the relationship is strengthened.', ARRAY['REL_006', 'OPP_015', 'NOTE_029', 'INT_048', 'RISK_048', 'RELM_144']::text[], 'SURFACE', 'This is the flagship contradictory-alignment scenario: strong public news paired with a genuinely weakening internal relationship, requiring synthesis across revenue, pipeline, a lost opportunity, and a note naming the competitor.'),
  ('GT_007', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_007'), (select signal_id from public.external_signals where evidence_code = 'SIG_007'), 'Declining revenue and pipeline, a lost financing mandate to a named competitor, and a negative note citing responsiveness as the cause -- with FX holding flat as a partial counterpoint', 'CONFIRMING', 'RELATIONSHIP_RISK', 'HIGH', 'Alphabet''s public setback is mirrored by a genuinely weakening internal relationship, with a specific, addressable root cause (response-time competitiveness) rather than a vague downturn.', ARRAY['REL_007', 'OPP_017', 'NOTE_033', 'INT_055', 'RISK_056', 'RELM_168']::text[], 'SURFACE', 'A second confirming risk case with a different evidence combination (responsiveness-driven loss vs. pricing-driven loss for Exxon) to test the agent isn''t pattern-matching on a single fixed evidence template.'),
  ('GT_008', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_008'), (select signal_id from public.external_signals where evidence_code = 'SIG_008'), 'Flat revenue, routine renewal in progress, and an explicit note that the leadership change has no bearing on the treasury relationship', 'NEUTRAL', 'NO_MATERIAL_IMPACT', 'LOW', 'The leadership transition is publicly significant for McKesson but has no material connection to the bank''s relationship, which remains flat, stable, and unaffected per the most recent client conversation.', ARRAY['REL_008', 'OPP_019', 'NOTE_037', 'INT_062', 'RISK_064', 'RELM_192']::text[], 'REVIEW', 'Tests whether the agent avoids over-indexing on a publicly significant event that internal evidence explicitly shows is not relevant to the relationship.'),
  ('GT_009', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_009'), (select signal_id from public.external_signals where evidence_code = 'SIG_009'), 'Small, thinly-documented relationship with very limited interaction and note history, and an explicit statement that the newest contact could not speak to the event', 'INSUFFICIENT', 'INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE', 'LOW', 'The relationship with Cencora is too thinly documented to produce a confident, personalized conclusion about how this public event affects the bank''s position -- the agent should recognize the evidence gap rather than speculate.', ARRAY['REL_009', 'OPP_021', 'NOTE_043', 'INT_072', 'RISK_072', 'RELM_216']::text[], 'REVIEW', 'A second insufficient-evidence case (paired with Walmart) driven by genuinely sparse relationship data rather than a topic mismatch, to test both failure modes of ''not enough evidence.'''),
  ('GT_010', (select company_id from public.company_master where company_code = 'CLI_010'), (select signal_id from public.external_signals where evidence_code = 'SIG_010'), 'Flat-to-slightly-declining core revenue, but a new high-value liquidity advisory opportunity directly requested by the client in response to the margin pressure', 'CONTRADICTORY', 'OPPORTUNITY', 'MEDIUM', 'Costco''s public margin pressure has created a genuine advisory opportunity rather than relationship risk -- the client is proactively seeking liquidity solutions, and the bank should pursue this as a chance to deepen the relationship.', ARRAY['REL_010', 'OPP_022', 'NOTE_047', 'INT_079', 'RISK_080', 'RELM_240']::text[], 'SURFACE', 'A second contrarian-opportunity case (negative headline, positive internal signal) with different mechanics than UnitedHealth''s, to test generalization rather than template matching.');
